Source: surge-xt
Section: sound
Priority: optional
Maintainer: Pau Aliagas <linuxnow@gmail.com>
Build-Depends: debhelper-compat (= 13), cmake (>= 3.22), ninja-build, g++, pkgconf, libasound2-dev, libjack-jackd2-dev,
 libx11-dev, libxrandr-dev, libxinerama-dev, libxcursor-dev, libxext-dev, libfreetype-dev, libfontconfig-dev,
 libcurl4-openssl-dev, libcairo2-dev, libxkbcommon-x11-dev, libxcb-cursor-dev, libxcb-keysyms1-dev,
 libxcb-util-dev, libgl-dev
Standards-Version: 4.6.2
Homepage: https://surge-synthesizer.github.io/
Rules-Requires-Root: no

Package: surge-xt
Section: metapackages
Architecture: any
Depends: surge-xt-clap (= ${binary:Version}), surge-xt-lv2 (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: hybrid synthesizer, CLAP and LV2 plugins
 Surge XT is a hybrid synthesizer: three oscillators per scene with
 wavetable, FM, ring modulation and the classic waveforms, two filters, a
 modulation matrix, and effects. This package installs both of its plugin
 formats.

Package: surge-xt-data
Architecture: all
Multi-Arch: foreign
Depends: ${misc:Depends}
Description: factory patches, wavetables and skins of Surge XT
 The data both Surge XT plugins read at start: the factory patches, the
 wavetables, the tuning files and the skins, in /usr/share/surge-xt.

Package: surge-xt-clap
Architecture: any
Depends: surge-xt-data (= ${source:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Surge XT as a CLAP plugin
 Surge XT as a CLAP instrument, installed in /usr/lib/clap where CLAP hosts,
 omx-clap-host among them, look.

Package: surge-xt-lv2
Architecture: any
Depends: surge-xt-data (= ${source:Version}), ${shlibs:Depends}, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Surge XT as an LV2 plugin
 Surge XT as an LV2 instrument, installed in /usr/lib/lv2 where LV2 hosts
 look.
